# Animation & Interaction

Warm daylight pages, with a dark stage reserved for the home glass panel and AR/VR scenes. Motion is part of the interface: cinematic transitions and fluid micro-interactions. Never swap pages or hover states instantly.

## Structural motion

Use spring physics for layout, panels, and page transitions. Do not use linear easing for structural UI.

```tsx
const spring = { type: "spring", stiffness: 100, damping: 15 } as const;

<motion.main
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 24 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  transition={spring}
>
```

## Pointer effects

Drive parallax and custom cursor tracking with `useMotionValue` and `useTransform`. Do not store pointer position in React state on every move.

```tsx
const x = useMotionValue(0);
const rotateY = useTransform(x, [-0.5, 0.5], [-8, 8]);
```
